{
  "title": "37: As-Saffat الصافات",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالصّٰٓفّٰتِ صَفًّا ۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAAFFAATE SAFFAA.\nBy the [angels] ranged in ranks,\nفَالزّٰجِرٰتِ زَجْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAZZAAJERAATE ZAJRAA.\nby the ones who drive [the clouds] vigorously,\nفَالتّٰلِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFATTAALEYAATE ZIKRAA.\nby the ones who recite the reminder:\nاِنَّ اِلٰهَكُمْ لَوَاحِدٌ ؕ‏(4)\nINNA ELAAHAKUM LA-WAAHED.\nindeed your God is certainly One,\nرَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ الْمَشَارِقِ ؕ‏(5)\nRABBUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA RABBUL MASHAAREQ.\nthe Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, and the Lord of the easts.\nاِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِيْنَةِ اۨلْكَوَاكِبِۙ‏(6)\nINNAA ZAYYANNAS SAMAAA-AD DUNYAA BE-ZEENATENIL KAWAAKEB.\nIndeed We have adorned the lowest heaven with the finery of the stars,\nوَحِفْظًا مِّنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّارِدٍۚ‏(7)\nWA HIFZAM MIN KULLE SHAYTAANIM MAARED.\nand to guard from any froward devil.\nلَّا يَسَّمَّعُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَلَاِ الْاَعْلٰى وَيُقْذَفُوْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَانِبٍۖ ‏(8)\nLAA YASSAMMA-O’ONA ELAL MALA-IL A-A’LAA WA YUQZAFOONA MIN KULLE JAANEB.\nThey do not eavesdrop on the Supernal Elite—they are shot at from every side,\nدُحُوْرًا  وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَّاصِبٌ  ۙ‏(9)\nDOHOORANW WA LAHUM A’ZAABUNW WAASEB.\nto drive them away, and there is a perpetual punishment for them—\nاِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ الْخَطْفَةَ فَاَتْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ‏(10)\nILLAA MAN KHATEFAL KHATFATA FA-ATBA-A’HU SHEHAABUN SAAQEB.\nexcept any who snatches a snatch, whereat a piercing flame pursues him.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَهُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمْ مَّنْ خَلَقْنَاؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ لَّازِبٍ‏(11)\nFASTAFTEHIM AHUM ASHADDO KHALQAN AM MAN KHALAQNAA, INNAA KHALAQNAAHUM MIN TEENIL LAAZEB.\nAsk them, is their creation more prodigious or [that of other creatures] that We have created? Indeed, We created them from a viscous clay.\nبَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُوْنَ‏(12)\nBAL A’JIBTA WA YASKHAROON.\nIndeed you wonder, while they engage in ridicule,\nوَاِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا لَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ZUKKEROO LAA YAZKOROON.\nand [even] when admonished do not take admonition,\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْا اٰيَةً يَّسْتَسْخِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA EZAA RA-AW AAYATAN-Y YASTASKHEROON.\nand when they see a sign they make it an object of ridicule,\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۖۚ‏(15)\nWA QAALOO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nand say, ‘This is nothing but plain magic!’\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(16)\nA-EZAA MITNAA WA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MAB-O’OSOON.\n‘What! When we are dead and have become dust and bones, shall we be resurrected?\nاَوَاٰبَآؤُنَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ‏(17)\nAWA AABAAA-ONAL AWWALOON.\nAnd our forefathers too?!’\nقُلْ نَعَمْ وَاَنْتُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَۚ‏(18)\nQUL NA-A’M WA ANTUM DAAKHEROON.\nSay, ‘Yes! And you will be utterly humble.’\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ فَاِذَا هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(19)\nFA-INNAMAA HEYA ZAJRATUNW WAAHEDATUN FA-EZAA HUM YANZOROON.\nIt will be only a single shout and, behold, they will look on,\nوَقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَا هٰذَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِ‏(20)\nWA QAALOO YAA WAYLANAA HAAZAA YAWMUD DEEN.\nand say, ‘Woe to us! This is the Day of Retribution!’\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(21)\nHAAZAA YAWMUL FASLIL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\n‘This is the Day of Judgement that you used to deny!’\nاُحْشُرُوا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا وَاَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(22)\nOHSHORUL LAZEENA ZALAMOO WA AZWAAJAHUM WA MAA KAANOO YA’BODOON.\n‘Muster the wrongdoers and their mates and what they used to worship\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَاهْدُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(23)\nMIN DOONIL LAAHE FAHDOOHUM ELAA SERAATIL JAHEEM.\nbesides Allah, and show them the way to hell!\nوَقِفُوْهُمْ اِنَّهُمْ مَّسْئُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(24)\nWA QEFOOHUM INNAHUM MAS-OOLOON.\n[But first] stop them! For they must be questioned.’\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُوْنَ‏(25)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANAASAROON.\n‘Why is it that you do not support one another [today]?’\nبَلْ هُمُ الْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُوْنَ‏(26)\nBAL HOMUL YAWMA MUSTASLEMOON.\n‘Indeed, they are [meek and] submissive today!’\nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(27)\nWA AQBALA BA’ZOHUM A’LAA BA’ZIN-Y YATASAAA-ALOON.\nSome of them will turn to others, questioning each other.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَاْتُوْنَنَا عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ‏(28)\nQAALOO INNAKUM KUNTUM TAATOONANAA A’NIL YAMEEN.\nThey will say, ‘Indeed you used to accost us peremptorily.’\nقَالُوْا بَلْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَۚ‏(29)\nQAALOO BAL LAM TAKOONOO MOAMENEEN.\nThey will answer, ‘No, you [yourselves] had no faith.\nوَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنِۚ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا طٰغِيْنَ‏(30)\nWA MAA KAANA LANAA A’LAYKUM MIN SULTAAN, BAL KUNTUM QAWMAN TAAGHEEN.\nWe had no authority over you. No, you [yourselves] were a rebellious lot.\nفَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآ ۖ اِنَّا لَذَآئِقُوْنَ‏(31)\nFA-HAQQA A’LAYNAA QAWLO RABBENAA, INNAA LA-ZAAA-EQOON.\nSo our Lord’s word became due against us that we shall indeed taste [the punishment].\nفَاَغْوَيْنٰكُمْ اِنَّا كُنَّا غٰوِيْنَ‏(32)\nFA-AGHWAYNAAKUM INNAA KUNNAA GHAAWEEN.\nSo we perverted you, for we were perverse [ourselves].’\nفَاِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nFA-INNAHUM YAWMA-EZIN FIL A’ZAABE MUSHTAREKOON.\nSo, that day they will share the punishment.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(34)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAF-A’LO BIL-MUJREMEEN.\nIndeed, that is how We deal with the guilty.\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُۙ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nINNAHUM KAANOO EZAA QEELA LAHUM LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO, YASTAKBEROON.\nIndeed, it was they who, when they were told, ‘There is no god except Allah,’ used to be disdainful,\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اَئِنَّا لَتٰرِكُوْۤا اٰلِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَّجْنُوْنٍ ؕ‏(36)\nWA YAQOOLOONA A-INNAA LA-TAAREKOO AALEHATENAA LE-SHAA-E’RIM MAJNOON.\nand [they would] say, ‘Shall we abandon our gods for a crazy poet?’\nبَلْ جَآءَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(37)\nBAL JAAA-A BIL-HAQQE WA SADDAQAL MURSALEEN.\nIndeed, he has brought [them] the truth, and confirmed the [earlier] apostles.\nاِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا الْعَذَابِ الْاَلِيْمِۚ‏(38)\nINNAKUM LA-ZAAA-EQUL A’ZAABIL ALEEM.\nIndeed you will taste the painful punishment,\nوَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA MAA TUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nand you will be requited only for what you used to do\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHIL MUKHLASEEN.\n—[all] except Allah’s exclusive servants.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(41)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAHUM RIZQUM MA’LOOM.\nFor such there is a known provision\nفَوَاكِهُۚ وَهُمْ مُّكْرَمُوْنَۙ‏(42)\nFAWAAKEH, WA HUM MUKRAMOON.\n—fruits—and they will be held in honour,\nفِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(43)\nFEE JANNAATIN NA-E’EM.\nin the gardens of bliss,\nعَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(44)\nA’LAA SORORIM MOTAQAABELEEN.\n[reclining] on couches, facing one another,\nيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِكَاْسٍ مِّنْ مَّعِيْنٍۢ ۙ‏(45)\nYOTAAFO A’LAYHIM BE-KAASIM MIM MA-E’EN.\nserved around with a cup, from a clear fountain,\nبَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(46)\nBAYZAAA-A LAZZATIL LISH-SHAAREBEEN.\nsnow-white, delicious to the drinkers,\nلَا فِيْهَا غَوْلٌ وَّلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنْزَفُوْنَ‏(47)\nLAA FEEHAA GHAWLUNW WA LAA HUM A’NHAA YUNZAFOON.\nwherein there will be neither headache nor will it cause them stupefaction,\nوَعِنْدَهُمْ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِ عِيْنٌۙ‏(48)\nWA I’NDAHUM QAASERAATUT TARFE E’EN.\nand with them will be maidens, of restrained glances with big [beautiful] eyes,\nكَاَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(49)\nKA-ANNAHUNNA BAYZUM MAKNOON.\nas if they were hidden ostrich eggs.\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(50)\nFA-AQBALA BA’ZOHUM A’LAA BA’ZIN-Y YATASAAA-ALOON.\nSome of them will turn to others, questioning each other.\nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ اِنِّىْ كَانَ لِىْ قَرِيْنٌۙ‏(51)\nQAALA QAAA-ELUM MINHUM INNEE KAANA LEE QAREEN.\nOne of them will say, ‘Indeed I had a companion\nيَقُوْلُ اَءِ نَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(52)\nYAQOOLO A-INNAKA LAMENAL MOSADDEQEEN.\nwho used to say, ‘‘Are you really among those who affirm\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَدِيْنُوْنَ‏(53)\nA-EZAA MITNAA WA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MADEENOON.\nthat when we have died and become dust and bones, we shall be brought to retribution?’’ ’\nقَالَ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّطَّلِعُوْنَ‏(54)\nQAALA HAL ANTUM MUTTALE-O’ON.\nHe will say, ‘Will you have a look?’\nفَاطَّلَعَ فَرَاٰهُ فِىْ سَوَآءِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(55)\nFAT-TALA-A’ FA-RA-AAHO FEE SAWAAA-IL JAHEEM.\nThen he will take a look and sight him in the middle of hell.\nقَالَ تَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كِدْتَّ لَتُرْدِيْنِۙ‏(56)\nQAALA TALLAAHE IN KITTA LATURDEEN.\nHe will say, ‘By Allah, you had almost ruined me!\nوَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA LAWLAA NE’MATO RABBEE LAKUNTO MENAL MOHZAREEN.\nHad it not been for my Lord’s blessing, I too would have been among those mustered [in hell]!’\nاَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِيْنَۙ‏(58)\nAFAMAA NAHNO BE-MAYYETEEN.\n‘Is it [true] that we shall not die [anymore],\nاِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا الْاُوْلٰى وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(59)\nILLAA MAWTATANAL OOLAA WA MAA NAHNO BE-MO-A’ZZABEEN.\naside from our earlier death, and that we shall not be punished?\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(60)\nINNA HAAZAA LAHOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nThis is indeed the supreme triumph!’\nلِمِثْلِ هٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعٰمِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nLE-MISLE HAAZAA FALYA’MALIL A’AMELOON.\nLet all workers work for the like of this!\nاَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا اَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّوْمِ‏(62)\nAZAALEKA KHAYRUN NOZOLAN AM SHAJARATUZ ZAQQOOM.\nIs this a better reception, or the Zaqqum tree?\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنٰهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(63)\nINNAA JA-A’LNAAHAA FITNATAL LIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nIndeed We have made it a punishment for the wrongdoers.\nاِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِىْۤ اَصْلِ الْجَحِيْمِۙ‏(64)\nINNAHAA SHAJARATUN TAKHROJO FEE ASLIL JAHEEM.\nIt is a tree that rises from the depths of hell.\nطَلْعُهَا كَاَنَّهٗ رُءُوْسُ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ‏(65)\nTAL-O’HAA KA-ANNAHU RO-OOSUSH SHAYAATEEN.\nIts spathes are as if they were devils’ heads.\nفَاِنَّهُمْ لَاٰكِلُوْنَ مِنْهَا فَمٰلِئُوْنَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُوْنَ ؕ‏(66)\nFA-INNAHUM LA-AAKELOONA MINHAA FA-MAALE-OONA MINHAL BOTOON.\nThey will eat from it and gorge with it their bellies.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍۚ‏(67)\nSUMMA INNA LAHUM A’LAYHAA LA-SHAWBAM MIN HAMEEM.\nOn top of that they will take a solution of scalding water.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَا۟اِلَى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(68)\nSUMMA INNA MARJE-A’HUM LA-ELAL JAHEEM.\nThen their retreat will be toward hell.\nاِنَّهُمْ اَلْفَوْا اٰبَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّيْنَۙ‏(69)\nINNAHUM ALFAW AABAAA-AHUM ZAALLEEN.\nThey had found their fathers astray,\nفَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُوْنَ‏(70)\nFAHUM A’LAA AASAAREHIM YOHRA-O’ON.\nyet they press onwards in their footsteps.\nوَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ اَكْثَرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(71)\nWA LAQAD ZALLA QABLAHUM AKSARUL AWWALEEN.\nMost of the former peoples went astray before them,\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ مُّنْذِرِيْنَ‏(72)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA FEEHIM MUNZEREEN.\nand We had certainly sent warners among them.\nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَۙ‏(73)\nFANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUNZAREEN.\nSo observe how was the fate of those who were warned\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(74)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHIL MUKHLASEEN.\n—[all] except Allah’s exclusive servants!\nوَلَقَدْ نَادٰٮنَا نُوْحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ الْمُجِيْبُوْنَ  ۖ‏(75)\nWA LAQAD NAADAANAA NOOHUN FALANE’MAL MOJEEBOON.\nCertainly Noah called out to Us, and how well did We respond!\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ  ۖ‏(76)\nWA NAJJAYNAAHO WA AHLAHU MENAL KARBIL A’ZEEM.\nWe delivered him and his family from their great distress,\nوَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهٗ هُمُ الْبٰقِيْنَ  ۖ‏(77)\nWA JA-A’LNAA ZURRIYYATAHU HOMUL BAAQEEN.\nand made his descendants the survivors,\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَ  ۖ‏(78)\nWA TARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AAKHEREEN.\nand left for him a good name among posterity:\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ فِى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(79)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA NOOHIN FIL A’ALAMEEN.\n‘Peace to Noah, throughout the nations!’\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(80)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus do We reward the virtuous.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(81)\nINNAHU MIN E’BAADENAL MOAMENEEN.\nHe is indeed one of Our faithful servants.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(82)\nSUMMA AGHRAQNAL AAKHAREEN.\nThen We drowned the rest.\nوَاِنَّ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ لَاِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(83)\nWA INNA MIN SHEE-A’TEHI LA-IBRAAHEEM.\nIndeed Abraham was among his followers,\nاِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهٗ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍ‏(84)\nIZ JAAA-A RABBAHU BE-QALBIN SALEEM.\nwhen he came to his Lord with a sound heart [untainted by sin].\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۚ‏(85)\nIZ QAALA LE-ABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAAZAA TA’BODOON.\nWhen he said to his father and his people, ‘What is it that you are worshiping?\nاَئِفْكًا اٰلِهَةً دُوْنَ اللّٰهِ تُرِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(86)\nA-IFKAN AALEHATAN DOONAL LAAHE TOREEDOON.\nIs it a lie, gods other than Allah, that you desire?\nفَمَا ظَنُّكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(87)\nFAMAA ZANNOKUM BE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThen what is your idea about the Lord of all the worlds?’\nفَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِى النُّجُوْمِۙ‏(88)\nFA-NAZARA NAZRATAN FIN NOJOOM.\nThen he made an observation of the stars\nفَقَالَ اِنِّىْ سَقِيْمٌ‏(89)\nFA-QAALA INNEE SAQEEM.\nand said, ‘Indeed I am sick!’\nفَتَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(90)\nFA-TAWALLAW A’NHO MUDBEREEN.\nSo they went away leaving him behind.\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اٰلِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَۚ‏(91)\nFA-RAAGHA ELAA AALEHATEHIM FA-QAALA ALAA TAAKOLOON.\nThen he stole away to their gods and said, ‘Will you not eat?\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(92)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANTEQOON.\nWhy do you not speak?’\nفَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِالْيَمِيْنِ‏(93)\nFA-RAAGHA A’LAYHIM ZARBAM BIL-YAMEEN.\nThen he attacked them, striking forcefully.\nفَاَقْبَلُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّوْنَ‏(94)\nFA-AQBALOO ELAYHE YAZIFFOON.\nThey came running towards him.\nقَالَ اَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مَا تَنْحِتُوْنَۙ‏(95)\nQAALA ATA’BODOONA MAA TANHETOON.\nHe said, ‘Do you worship what you have yourselves carved,\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM WA MAA TA’MALOON.\nwhen Allah has created you and whatever you make?’\nقَالُوا ابْنُوْا لَهٗ بُنْيَانًا فَاَلْقُوْهُ فِى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(97)\nQAALUB NOO LAHU BUNYAANAN FA-ALQOOHO FIL JAHEEM.\nThey said, ‘Build a structure for him and cast him into a huge fire.’\nفَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَسْفَلِيْنَ‏(98)\nFA-ARAADOO BEHI KAYDAN FA-JA-A’LNAAHOMUL ASFALEEN.\nSo they sought to outwit him, but We made them the lowermost.\nوَقَالَ اِنِّىْ ذَاهِبٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(99)\nWA QAALA INNEE ZAAHEBUN ELAA RABBEE SAYAHDEEN.\nHe said, ‘Indeed I am going toward my Lord, who will guide me.’\nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(100)\nRABBE HAB LEE MENAS SAALEHEEN.\n‘My Lord! Give me [an heir], one of the righteous.’\nفَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِغُلٰمٍ حَلِيْمٍ‏(101)\nFA-BASH-SHARNAAHO BE-GHOLAAMIN HALEEM.\nSo We gave him the good news of a forbearing son.\nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْىَ قَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى فِى الْمَنَامِ اَنِّىْۤ اَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرٰىؕ قَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nFALAMMAA BALAGHA MA-A’HUS SA’YA QAALA YAA BONAYYA INNEE ARAA FIL MANAAME ANNEE AZBAHOKA FANZUR MAAZAA TARAA, QAALA YAA ABATIF A’L MAA TOAMAR, SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAS SAABEREEN.\nWhen he was old enough to assist in his endeavour, he said, ‘My son! I see in dreams that I am sacrificing you. See what you think.’ He said, ‘Father! Do whatever you have been commanded. If Allah wishes, you will find me to be patient.’\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهٗ لِلْجَبِيْنِۚ‏(103)\nFALAMMAA ASLAMAA WA TALLAHU LIL-JABEEN.\nSo when they had both surrendered [to Allah’s will], and he had laid him down on his forehead,\nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ اَنْ يّٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُۙ‏(104)\nWA NAADAYNAAHO AN-Y YAA IBRAAHEEM.\nWe called out to him, ‘O Abraham!\nقَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّءْيَا  ۚ اِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(105)\nQAD SADDAQTAR ROAYAA, INNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nYou have indeed fulfilled your vision! Thus indeed do We reward the virtuous!\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلٰٓؤُا الْمُبِيْنُ‏(106)\nINNA HAAZAA LAHOWAL BALAAA-UL MOBEEN.\nThis was indeed a manifest test.’\nوَفَدَيْنٰهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(107)\nWA FADAYNAAHO BE-ZIBHIN A’ZEEM.\nThen We ransomed him with a great sacrifice,\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۖ‏(108)\nWA TARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AAKHEREEN.\nand left for him a good name in posterity:\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‏(109)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA IBRAAHEEM.\n‘Peace be to Abraham!’\nكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(110)\nKAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus do We reward the virtuous.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(111)\nINNAHU MIN E’BAADENAL MOAMENEEN.\nHe is indeed one of Our faithful servants.\nوَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِاِسْحٰقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(112)\nWA BASH-SHARNAAHO BE-ISHAAQA NABIYYAM MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We gave him the good news of [the birth of] Isaac, a prophet, one of the righteous.\nوَبٰرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلٰٓى اِسْحٰقَؕ وَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَّظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ مُبِيْنٌ‏(113)\nWA BAARAKNAA A’LAYHE WA A’LAA ISHAAQ, WA MIN ZURRIYYATEHEMAA MOHSENUNW WA ZAALEMUL LE-NAFSEHI MOBEEN.\nAnd We blessed him and Isaac. Among their descendants [some] are virtuous, and [some] who manifestly wrong themselves.\nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَۚ‏(114)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAA MOOSAA WA HAAROON.\nCertainly We favoured Moses and Aaron,\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِۚ‏(115)\nWA NAJJAYNAAHOMAA WA QAWMAHOMAA MENAL KARBIL A’ZEEM.\nand delivered them and their people from their great distress,\nوَنَصَرْنٰهُمْ فَكَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَۚ‏(116)\nWA NASARNAAHUM FA-KAANOO HOMUL GHAALEBEEN.\nand We helped them so that they became the victors.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمَا الْكِتٰبَ الْمُسْتَبِيْنَۚ‏(117)\nWA AATAYNAAHOMAL KETAABAL MUSTABEEN.\nWe gave them the illuminating scripture\nوَهَدَيْنٰهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۚ‏(118)\nWA HADAYNAAHOMAS SERAATAL MUSTAQEEM.\nand guided them to the straight path,\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(119)\nWA TARAKNAA A’LAYHEMAA FIL AAKHEREEN.\nand left for them a good name in posterity.\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(120)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA MOOSAA WA HAAROON.\n‘Peace be to Moses and Aaron!’\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do We reward the virtuous.\nاِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(122)\nINNAHOMAA MIN E’BAADENAL MOAMENEEN.\nThey are indeed among Our faithful servants.\nوَاِنَّ اِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(123)\nWA INNA ILYAASA LAMENAL MURSALEEN.\nIndeed Ilyas was one of the apostles.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LE-QAWMEHI ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen he said to his people, ‘Will you not be Godwary?\nاَتَدْعُوْنَ بَعْلًا وَّتَذَرُوْنَ اَحْسَنَ الْخٰلِقِيْنَۙ‏(125)\nATAD-O’ONA BA’LANW WA TAZAROONA AHSANAL KHAALEQEEN.\nDo you invoke Baal and abandon the best of creators,\nاللّٰهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(126)\nALLAAHA RABBAKUM WA RABBA AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nAllah, your Lord and Lord of your forefathers?,’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(127)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-INNAHUM LA-MOHZAROON.\nthey impugned him. So they will indeed be mustered [in hell]\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(128)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHIL MUKHLASEEN.\n—[all] except Allah’s exclusive servants.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(129)\nWA TARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AAKHEREEN.\nWe left for him a good name in posterity.\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِلْ يَاسِيْنَ‏(130)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA IL YAASEEN.\n‘Peace be to Ilyas!’\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(131)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do We reward the virtuous.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\nINNAHU MIN E’BAADENAL MOAMENEEN.\nHe is indeed one of Our faithful servants.\nوَاِنَّ لُوْطًا لَّمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(133)\nWA INNA LOOTAL LAMENAL MURSALEEN.\nIndeed Lot was one of the apostles.\nاِذْ نَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(134)\nIZ NAJJAYNAAHO WA AHLAHU AJMA-E’EN.\nWhen We delivered him and all his family,\nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(135)\nILLAA A’JOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nexcepting an old woman among those who remained behind,\nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(136)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAL AAKHAREEN.\nWe destroyed the rest.\nوَاِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مُّصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nWA INNAKUM LATAMURROONA A’LAYHIM MUSBEHEEN.\nIndeed you pass by them at dawn\nوَبِالَّيْلِؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(138)\nWA BIL-LAYL, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nand at night. Do you not exercise your reason?\nوَاِنَّ يُوْنُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(139)\nWA INNA YOONOSA LAMENAL MURSALEEN.\nIndeed Jonah was one of the apostles.\nاِذْ اَبَقَ اِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِۙ‏(140)\nIZ ABAQA ELAL FULKIL MASH-HOON.\nWhen he absconded toward the laden ship,\nفَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِيْنَۚ‏(141)\nFA-SAAHAMA FA-KAANA MENAL MUDHAZEEN.\nhe drew lots with them and was the one to be condemned [as one to be thrown overboard].\nفَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوْتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌ‏(142)\nFALTAQAMAHUL HOOTO WA HOWA MOLEEM.\nThen the fish swallowed him while he was blameworthy.\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِيْنَۙ‏(143)\nFALAWLAA ANNAHU KAANA MENAL MOSABBEHEEN.\nHad he not been one of those who celebrate Allah’s glory,\nلَلَبِثَ فِىْ بَطْنِهٖۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَۚ‏(144)\nLALABESA FEE BATNEHI ELAA YAWME YUB-A’SOON.\nhe would have surely remained in its belly till the day they will be resurrected.\nفَنَبَذْنٰهُ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيْمٌۚ‏(145)\nFA-NABAZNAAHO BIL-A’RAAA-E WA HOWA SAQEEM.\nThen We cast him on a bare shore, and he was sick.\nوَاَنْۢبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّنْ يَّقْطِيْنٍۚ‏(146)\nWA AMBATNAA A’LAYHE SHAJARATAM MIN-Y YAQTEEN.\nSo We made a gourd plant grow above him.\nوَاَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى مِائَةِ اَلْفٍ اَوْ يَزِيْدُوْنَۚ‏(147)\nWA ARSALNAAHO ELAA ME-ATE ALFIN AW YAZEEDOON.\nWe sent him to a [community of] hundred thousand or more,\nفَاٰمَنُوْا فَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍؕ‏(148)\nFA-AAMANOO FA-MATTA’NAAHUM ELAA HEEN.\nand they believed [in him]. So We provided for them for a while.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَلِرَبِّكَ الْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ الْبَنُوْنَۙ‏(149)\nFASTAFTEHIM ALE-RABBEKAL BANAATO WA LAHOMUL BANOON.\nAsk them, are daughters to be for your Lord while sons are to be for them?\nاَمْ خَلَقْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ اِنَاثًا وَّهُمْ شٰهِدُوْنَ‏(150)\nAM KHALAQNAL MALAAA-EKATA ENAASANW WA HUM SHAAHEDOON.\nDid We create the angels females while they were present?\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنْ اِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(151)\nALAA INNAHUM MIN IFKEHIM LAYAQOOLOON.\nBe aware that it is out of their mendacity that they say,\nوَلَدَ اللّٰهُۙ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(152)\nWALADAL LAAHO, WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\n‘Allah has begotten [offsprings],’ and they indeed speak a falsehood.\nاَصْطَفَى الْبَنَاتِ عَلَى الْبَنِيْنَؕ‏(153)\nASTAFAL BANAATE A’LAL BANEEN.\nHas He preferred daughters to sons?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(154)\nMAA LAKUM, KAYFA TAHKOMOON.\nWhat is the matter with you? How do you judge?\nاَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَۚ‏(155)\nAFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nWill you not then take admonition?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطٰنٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(156)\nAM LAKUM SULTAANUM MOBEEN.\nDo you have a manifest authority?\nفَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبِكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(157)\nFAATOO BE-KETAABEKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThen produce your scripture, should you be truthful.\nوَجَعَلُوْا بَيْنَهٗ وَبَيْنَ الْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ الْجِنَّةُ اِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(158)\nWA JA-A’LOO BAYNAHU WA BAYNAL JINNATE NASABAA, WA LAQAD A’LEMATIL JINNATO INNAHUM LA-MOHZAROON.\nAnd they have set up a kinship between Him and the jinn, while the jinn certainly know that they will be presented [before Him].\nسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(159)\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOON.\nClear is Allah of whatever they allege [about Him]\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(160)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHIL MUKHLASEEN.\n—[all] except Allah’s exclusive servants.\nفَاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(161)\nFA-INNAKUM WA MAA TA’BODOON.\nIndeed you and what you worship\nمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفٰتِنِيْنَۙ‏(162)\nMAA ANTUM A’LAYHE BE-FAATENEEN.\ncannot mislead [anyone] about Him,\nاِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(163)\nILLAA MAN HOWA SAALIL JAHEEM.\nexcept someone who is bound for hell.\nوَمَا مِنَّاۤ اِلَّا لَهٗ مَقَامٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(164)\nWA MAA MINNAA ILLAA LAHU MAQAAMUM MA’LOOM.\n‘There is none among us but has a known place.\nوَّاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّآفُّوْنَۚ‏(165)\nWA INNAA LANAHNUS SAAFFOON.\nIt is we who are the ranged ones.\nوَاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA INNAA LANAHNUL MOSABBEHOON.\nIt is we who celebrate Allah’s glory.’\nوَاِنْ كَانُوْا لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(167)\nWA IN KAANOO LAYAQOOLOON.\nThey indeed, used to say,\nلَوْ اَنَّ عِنْدَنَا ذِكْرًا مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(168)\nLAW ANNA I’NDANAA ZIKRAM MENAL AWWALEEN.\n‘Had we possessed a Reminder from our predecessors,\nلَكُنَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(169)\nLAKUNNAA E’BAADAL LAAHIL MUKHLASEEN.\nwe would have surely been Allah’s exclusive servants.’\nفَكَفَرُوْا بِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(170)\nFA-KAFAROO BEHI FASAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nBut they disbelieved it [when it came to them]. Soon they will know!\nوَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(171)\nWA LAQAD SABAQAT KALEMATONAA LE-E’BAADENAL MURSALEEN.\nCertainly Our decree has gone beforehand in favour of Our servants, the apostles,\nاِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ الْمَنْصُوْرُوْنَ ‏(172)\nINNAHUM LAHOMUL MANSOOROON.\nthat they will indeed receive [Allah’s] help,\nوَاِنَّ جُنْدَنَا لَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(173)\nWA INNA JUNDANAA LAHOMUL GHAALEBOON.\nand indeed Our hosts will be the victors.\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(174)\nFA-TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo leave them alone for a while,\nوَاَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(175)\nWA ABSIRHUM FASAWFA YUBSEROON.\nand watch them; soon they will see [the truth of the matter]!\nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(176)\nAFABE-A’ZAABENAA YASTA’JELOON.\nDo they seek to hasten Our punishment?\nفَاِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَآءَ صَبَاحُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(177)\nFA-EZAA NAZALA BE-SAAHATEHIM FA-SAAA-A SABAAHUL MUNZAREEN.\nBut when it descends in their courtyard it will be a dismal dawn for those who had been warned.\nوَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(178)\nWA TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo leave them alone for a while,\nوَّاَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(179)\nWA ABSIR FASAWFA YUBSEROON.\nand watch; soon they will see!\nسُبْحٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ الْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۚ‏(180)\nSUBHAANA RABBEKA RABBIL I’ZZATE AMMAA YASEFOON.\nClear is your Lord, the Lord of Might, of whatever they allege [concerning Him].\nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۚ‏(181)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAL MURSALEEN. \nPeace be to the apostles!\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(182)\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAll praise belongs to Allah, Lord of all the worlds.",
  "merits": "There are 182 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the total number of Jinn and Shayateen that exist. The reciter of this Surah is protected from Shaitan and is safe from falling into disbelief and Shirk. His angels who record his deeds will testify for him on the Day of Judgement that he was from among those who believed in the Prophets of Allah (s.w.t.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that reciting Surah as-Saaffaat on every Friday keeps one safe from all types of calamities. His sustenance will increase and his life, wealth and children will be protected from the evil designs of Shaitan and the tyrant rulers of the time. If one dies soon after reciting this Surah, he will die the death of a martyr; he will be raised on the Day of Judgement together with the martyrs and will enter Jannah with them."
